{"Banga": [{"id": "BaMga", "headword": "भंग", "headword_slp1": "BaMga", "fold": "Banga", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Bhaṅga, ‘hemp,’ is mentioned in the Atharvaveda. In the Rigveda it is an epithet of soma, presumably in the sense of ‘intoxicating,’ which then came to designate hemp.\nFoot notes xi. 6, 15; conceivably in śāṅkhāyana Āraṇyaka, xii. 14, but not probably.\nix. 61, 13.\nSchrader, Prehistoric Antiquities, 299.\nHence the modern ‘Bang’ or Bhang,’ an intoxicant made from the dried leaves and small stalks of hemp, taken either by smoking or by eating when mixed up into a sweetmeat.\nCf. Zimmer, Altindisches Leben, 68; Grierson, Indian Antiquary, 23, 260; Yule and Burnell, Hobson-Jobson, s.v. Bang.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["bhaMga", "bhanga", "bhaṅga", "भङ्ग", "భంగ", "భఙ్గ", "ಭಂಗ", "ಭಙ್ಗ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["bhaMga", "bhanga", "bhaṅga", "BaNga", "భంగ", "భఙ్గ", "ಭಂಗ", "ಭಙ್ಗ"]}], "Bangasvina": [{"id": "BaMgASvina", "headword": "भंगाश्विन", "headword_slp1": "BaMgASvina", "fold": "Bangasvina", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Bhaṅgāśvina is the name of the father of Ṛtuparna in the baudhāyana śrauta sūtra. In the Mahābhārata he is called Bhāṅgāsuri. In the Āpastamba śrauta sūtra mention is made of ṛtuparṇa-Kayovadhī as the Bhaṅgyaśvinau.\nFoot notes xx. 12.\niii. 2745.\nxxi. 20; Caland, Zeitschrift der Deutschen Morgenländischen Gesellschaft, 57, 745.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["bhaMgaashvina", "bhangaashvina", "bhaṅgāśvina", "भङ्गाश्विन", "భంగాశ్విన", "భఙ్గాశ్విన", "ಭಂಗಾಶ್ವಿನ", "ಭಙ್ಗಾಶ್ವಿನ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["bhaMgaashvina", "bhangaashvina", "bhaṅgāśvina", "BaNgASvina", "భంగాశ్విన", "భఙ్గాశ్విన", "ಭಂಗಾಶ್ವಿನ", "ಭಙ್ಗಾಶ್ವಿನ"]}], "Bangya-sravas": [{"id": "BaMgya-Sravas", "headword": "भंग्य-श्रवस्", "headword_slp1": "BaMgya-Sravas", "fold": "Bangya-sravas", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-k